{"seq":13,"trial_id":"matrix-mu-2026-11/qm-pi-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T07:57:18.843Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"e4a40aa1d7e1bd2a14d85bfbb641087bd2ef70039d4df98c99104921683fa8f9","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492.** Source: *Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth* (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at Dock Doors 14–18 at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift got through the gate without manual help. The note also has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n2. **#4419.** Source: *Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)* (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea also logged this one. The gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on the third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell you when it was opened.\n\nSome things I left out:\n- Moss's other Quarrendon notes (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers.\n- The ticket numbers in Moss's Central handoff digest (#4409, #4412, FR-882) are for Central accounts, not Quarrendon.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company. They aren't a Pemberline customer, so don't mix them up with Quarrendon.\n\nI only looked through Moss's shared files. I didn't search channels for other ticket mentions."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DMATRIX0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
